import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"TODO","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"TODO","type":"task","date":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/TODO.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/TODO.md"}`),a={name:`graphopt/project/TODO.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="todo" tabindex="-1">TODO <a class="header-anchor" href="#todo" aria-label="Permalink to “TODO”">​</a></h1><h2 id="high-—-adr-0159-dissolve-the-optimizer-domains-into-ext-tools" tabindex="-1">HIGH — ADR-0159: dissolve the optimizer domains into <code>ext</code> tools <a class="header-anchor" href="#high-—-adr-0159-dissolve-the-optimizer-domains-into-ext-tools" aria-label="Permalink to “HIGH — ADR-0159: dissolve the optimizer domains into ext tools”">​</a></h2><p>Adopted on three triggers, not a date (<code>host/project/adrs/0159-…</code>):</p><ul class="task-list-container"><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-0" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-0"> a caller that is <strong>not the researcher</strong> needs the capability</label></li><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-1" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-1"> the domain&#39;s public surface <strong>unchanged for four weeks</strong></label></li><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-2" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-2"> the <strong>referee is shared</strong> (<code>bench/benchkit</code> usable by any domain)</label></li></ul><p>When all three hold: wrap, do not rewrite (Python core behind a port/adapter, thin ext command). Naming: <code>opt-*</code> family; a third member only on the rule of three.</p><ul class="task-list-container"><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-3" checked="checked" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-3"><strong>Registry gap — fixed.</strong> <code>host/scripts/gen-adr-index.py</code> built the index only from the hand-maintained <code>docs-split.yaml</code>, so newly written ADRs were invisible (0158 and 0159 both missing while present and committed). It now unions the manifest with a directory scan: 151 → 164 ADRs, both present. The docs hub&#39;s <code>adrs/handl.md</code> picks them up on regeneration; <code>adrs/index.md</code> is org-scoped by design and correctly excludes them.</label></li></ul><h2 id="high-—-m1-the-machine-finds-the-kernel-not-me-five-items-5-days" tabindex="-1">HIGH — M1: the machine finds the kernel, not me (five items, ~5 days) <a class="header-anchor" href="#high-—-m1-the-machine-finds-the-kernel-not-me-five-items-5-days" aria-label="Permalink to “HIGH — M1: the machine finds the kernel, not me (five items, ~5 days)”">​</a></h2><p>Lab-form per ADR-0159 (no ext wrapper yet); ADR-0160 allocates the IR.</p><p>Target: <code>qgemv</code> <strong>and</strong> <code>gate_proj</code> generated from <code>Term</code>s, exact against <code>awq_gemm</code>, at least one within the hand kernel&#39;s 58.9 µs cold.</p><ul class="task-list-container"><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-4" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-4"><strong>ADR-0160</strong> in <code>opt-kernel</code> (today <code>kernelopt</code>): the kernel IR is <code>Term</code> + kit-declared ops</label></li><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-5" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-5"><strong><code>lib-kernel-ir</code></strong> (public): nine ops, grades, costs, one torch denotation per op — the vocabulary, and the equality reference</label></li><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-6" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-6"><strong><code>compile-triton</code></strong> (Rust, <code>compile-*</code> family): <code>Term</code> → Triton, <code>qgemv</code> + <code>gate_proj</code> × <code>split_k ∈ {1,2,4,8}</code></label></li><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-7" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-7"><strong>Equality gate</strong> vs <code>awq_gemm</code> in <code>graphopt/bench</code> — cosine ≥ 0.9999 on every variant, inside the timing path</label></li><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-8" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-8"><strong>Search driver</strong> in <code>kernelopt</code>: enumerate <code>Term</code>s → gate → roofline bound → deploy-referee measure → best kernel + routing row</label></li></ul><p><strong>Kill criterion:</strong> if a fixed lowering cannot match hand-written Triton on <code>qgemv</code> and reach parity on <code>gate_proj</code>, generalising is wasted work — keep hand-writing kernels, use the search only for configs.</p><p><strong>M1.5 before any breadth</strong> (formats × shapes): compile cache + pruning by roofline bound. Breadth multiplies candidates and is otherwise rate-limited by <code>triton.jit</code>, not by ideas.</p><h2 id="done-—-2026-10-27-kernel-margin-valid" tabindex="-1">Done — 2026-10-27 (kernel margin, valid) <a class="header-anchor" href="#done-—-2026-10-27-kernel-margin-valid" aria-label="Permalink to “Done — 2026-10-27 (kernel margin, valid)”">​</a></h2><ul class="task-list-container"><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-9" checked="checked" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-9"> int4 GEMV beats <code>awq_gemm</code> cold on 3 of 4 layer shapes — <strong>2.96× / 1.52× / 1.35×</strong>, exact (<code>docs/reports/p14_correct_splitk.md</code>)</label></li><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-10" checked="checked" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-10"> substituted into vLLM: <strong>token-identical, −29.2 %</strong> end-to-end, 25/25 paired rounds (<code>docs/reports/p18_e2e_29pct.md</code>)</label></li><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-11" checked="checked" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-11"> deploy-regime referee as tested library (<code>bench/benchkit/regime.py</code>)</label></li><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-12" checked="checked" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-12"> three retractions published: fake 3.3× (fp16 atomics), fake −3.1 % (too few rounds), fake −28.5 % (AWQ nibble order)</label></li></ul><h2 id="active-—-high-priority-the-open-questions-post-plan-0032" tabindex="-1">Active — HIGH PRIORITY (the open questions, post-plan-0032) <a class="header-anchor" href="#active-—-high-priority-the-open-questions-post-plan-0032" aria-label="Permalink to “Active — HIGH PRIORITY (the open questions, post-plan-0032)”">​</a></h2><ul class="task-list-container"><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-13" checked="checked" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-13"><strong>Q3 — multi-step credit.</strong> <strong>Measured (2026-10-21).</strong><code>credit_chain</code> curriculum (<code>c59eaeb</code>, <code>docs/results_credit_chain.md</code>): learned arms DO close enabling chains unpreminted (neural → ceiling ~200 eps, linear-greedy 100%, advantage 71% sampled); honest break only at low chain density (k=16: linear-greedy collapses myopic, advantage fails) — the binding constraint is candidate density, not the credit mechanism.</label></li><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-14" checked="checked" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-14"><strong>Q2 — new algorithms (Strassen-class).</strong> <strong>Measured — NO-GO (2026-10-21).</strong> <code>bilinear</code> domain (<code>86115a7</code>+<code>9121617</code>, <code>docs/results_strassen.md</code>): board provably expresses Strassen (scripted → verified rank 7, 29 moves); playbook/ random/linear all stall at rank 8 — the ~15-move coordinated valley is beyond one-step lookahead. Follow-up: MCTS/ planner arm (in-flight) — does lookahead close the valley?</label></li><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-15" checked="checked" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-15"><strong>Q1 — unnamed structure on real corpora.</strong> <strong>Arm executed (2026-10-21).</strong> <code>overnight.py --corpus zoo-real --compose</code> landed (<code>863825c</code>/<code>6eb949d</code>/<code>04201f2</code>/<code>1000ffd</code>): real-subterm minting + bind-gate + emit-time RHS sanity (a real substrate bug: bare-<code>Exception</code> catch conflated can&#39;t-eval with eval-failed — fixed in eqsat <code>2d6e4eb</code>). Full-corpus funnel: 53 modules, 87 viable mints, <strong>0 machine-originals</strong> — honest zero; shallow single-step mints are all known-art. <strong>Re-opened and re-answered (2026-10-25): the zero was a <em>vocabulary</em> wall, not a search wall</strong> — let the mint name new primitives and <strong>21/21</strong> admitted folds are machine-original (then 48/48 deeper; 57 shipped ops, depths 1–3). The lever was never guarded composites. Retro: <code>project/retros/vocabulary-growth-2026-10-25.md</code>.</label></li><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-16" checked="checked" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-16"><strong>Q4 — scale.</strong> <strong>Measured (2026-10-21).</strong> <code>scale_ladder</code> (<code>b534bce</code>, <code>docs/reports/results_scale_ladder.md</code>): three distinct walls — matcher time ~11k unrolled nodes (&gt;445 s), verify-forward RAM (17.2 GB fp64 attn at T=4096; the e-graph itself sat in 0.2 s), fp64 overflow (RWKV exp at T≥1024). Symbolic blocks are T-invariant in the e-graph — substrate scales; the referee&#39;s real-env eval is the wall.</label></li><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-17" checked="checked" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-17"><strong>Q5 — self-modifying game.</strong> <strong>Measured — NULL, sharpened (2026-10-21).</strong> <code>transfer</code> probe (kernelopt <code>5994c71</code>): priors are <em>spec</em>-bound, not domain-bound — 10/12 foreign pairs can&#39;t enumerate a move; <code>META_SPEC</code> genuinely transfers across meta/joint/torch/gen (shared vocabulary). Kernel-side novelty sieve: in-flight.</label></li></ul><h2 id="active" tabindex="-1">Active <a class="header-anchor" href="#active" aria-label="Permalink to “Active”">​</a></h2><ul class="task-list-container"><li class="task-list-item"><p><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-18" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-18"> Meta-arena Q3 (<code>project/plans/0021-meta-arena.md</code>) — <strong>measured, partially answered.</strong> Cold linear REINFORCE beats scripted on mean reward (−0.04 vs −0.10 at 2000 episodes) only via the degenerate extract-early policy; the composed declare→handle line was unreachable by sampling until the <code>claim(tag)</code> option move fused it (claim→extract wins silu 2→1 on held-out boards, +0.52 payouts) — reachability fixed, consolidation by the memoryless policy still open. Retro: <code>project/retros/meta-arena-player.md</code>. Next levers: curriculum boards, imitation warm-start, richer policy.</label></p></li><li class="task-list-item"><p><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-19" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-19"> Generated kernels (<code>genkernel</code>) — <strong>the novelty question, measured.</strong> Handler entries minted for elementwise subterms the shipped HANDLERS never named; <code>torch.compile</code>&#39;d bindings; gen sink supports+lowers them; <code>claim</code> binds them — the board&#39;s vocabulary grows with lowerings it built. The concrete-soundness fix this forced (<code>_canon_concrete</code>, <code>claim_tags</code>) is a real correction: skeleton-level coverage could bind mismatched kernel semantics. <code>play --domain gen --probe</code>: <code>bigfuse</code> (6-op chain) → <code>claim(gen_0)</code> → verified module at <strong>2.87× vs eager</strong> (6.1× at 256×1024); 2-op fusions honestly lose (~0.86×, compiled-call overhead). Retro: <code>project/retros/gen-kernels.md</code>. Next: size-guarded claim offers, multi-claim composition, attr-bearing/reduction bodies.</label></p></li></ul><h2 id="deferred" tabindex="-1">Deferred <a class="header-anchor" href="#deferred" aria-label="Permalink to “Deferred”">​</a></h2><ul class="task-list-container"><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-20" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-20"><code>plan 0002</code> leftovers — Phase E recognizer consolidation (law-side e-class bindings vs lowerer-side extracted terms — substrates genuinely differ, revisit only if a shared kernel emerges); plan-dict typing stays dict-of-any.</label></li></ul><h2 id="tech-debt-to-fix" tabindex="-1">Tech debt to fix <a class="header-anchor" href="#tech-debt-to-fix" aria-label="Permalink to “Tech debt to fix”">​</a></h2><ul class="task-list-container"><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-21" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-21"><strong>Vendored probe code</strong> — copied third-party code in <code>bench/drivers/probes/</code> (and <code>bench/limits/registry.py</code> duplicated into kernelopt during the split). Replace with a declared dep/submodule or delete if dead.</label></li><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-22" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-22"><strong>Import-time domain registration</strong> — domains seat themselves via import side-effects (<code>mlopt_kernel.play</code> mutating <code>DOMAINS</code>/registry on import). Replace with explicit registration at call site.</label></li><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-23" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-23"><strong>Pinned test counts</strong> — tests asserting literal rule/law/bank counts (<code>test_prior_art</code>, <code>test_laws_structure</code> totals, <code>AGENTS.md</code> counts). Replace with derived counts or invariant-based assertions so bank growth doesn&#39;t churn tests.</label></li><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-24" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-24"><strong>radon baseline</strong> — <code>bilinear_game.py</code> flagged on clean main; regenerate <code>scripts/complexity_baseline.json</code> or justify.</label></li><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-25" checked="checked" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-25"><s><strong>Kernel-prim domain-draw gate</strong></s> — done 2026-10-27 (<code>handler_synth.SHAPE_REFUSALS</code>): the draw raises two torch refusals for one blind metavar (broadcast 64-vs-128 at dim 2, then <code>split_with_sizes</code> to 192 vs [64, 64]). Both are named and the entry is skipped, so the mint runs. A bounded window now returns <strong>2 candidates / 29 shapes mined / 0 unevaluable</strong> in 2 s; the 27-min zero was this abort, not an empty vocabulary.</label></li><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-26" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-26"><em><em>synop</em> real delivery</em>* — <code>docs/reports/prim_delivery.md</code> measured: folds compress terms (6993→4353 ops on GLA-large) but the spec-walk binding (<code>genkernel._eval_spec</code>) loses to spelled eager wall-clock on every clean case; the cost-model 0.5–0.8× pay is not delivered. Real delivery needs a fused-body codegen path for minted ops, not a spec interpreter. <strong>First step, measured 2026-10-27:</strong> the mint does register its ops (<code>mlopt_kernel.sink._table()</code> 84→86, <code>ksynop_9e3cb9a03a</code>, <code>ksynop_efc263c3dd</code>), but the zoo sweep&#39;s delivery path is <code>play.gen_probe → _gen_board(case)</code> and that board&#39;s bank comes from <code>genkernel</code> — it never reads the sink table. Teach <code>_gen_board</code> to merge the minted <code>ksynop_*</code> folds into its bank, then re-sweep the 46 losing zoo rows (median 0.979×).</label></li><li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" class="task-list-item-checkbox" id="task-item-27" disabled="disabled"><label class="task-list-item-label" for="task-item-27"><strong>ADR-0157 fragment-tower migration</strong> — local plan in <code>project/plans/0033-fragment-tower.md</code> + host ADR-0157; phases 0–5 (fragment dir → differential backend → denotations as models → fragment-emitting mint → fragment-move play → handl-native saturation).</label></li></ul>`,22)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};